From c4ffff6c0ec4f510ba6d44e4d69eca44ad98cdca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ObeseCatLord <6099645+ObeseCatLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 11:20:35 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] recomp: EE MMI halfword multiplies, 128-bit HI/LO transfers,
 exchanges

PMULTH/PMADDH/PMSUBH summed all eight products into one 64-bit value;
the EE keeps each product in its own word of LO/HI (128 bits: lo/hi plus
lo1/hi1) and returns {LO.w0, HI.w0, LO.w2, HI.w2} in rd. The games use
PMULTH for squared distances (Zettai 0x139958, Eigou 1 0x13a630).
PMFHL/PMTHL ignored the upper halves and had the wrong word order.
PEXEH, PEXCH, PEXEW and PROT3W used the wrong shuffles, PADDUH/PSUBUH
did not saturate, and PSLLH/PSRLH/PSRAH used all five bits of sa.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
